0-85c2-4432-a5d0-3737739e6966","position":{"commit_sha":"0738ba1d1a5af1b8ccb34726f5315af5424f4698","position":"1785771992095638001-e897e6c0-85c2-4432-a5d0-3737739e6966"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"9ecfba78b6523b7e8b0c956bf93fafc6908e9ecac69fb38bdfe67eacc8aa173d","event_uuid":"2576303f-2238-4667-9215-17155e477a46","position":{"commit_sha":"0738ba1d1a5af1b8ccb34726f5315af5424f4698","position":"1785771992597643001-2576303f-2238-4667-9215-17155e477a46"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e9dc76bddbb790f1c0a8cfbc9c01d206642f75d9a0fa07f84a6c8c58107bc137","event_uuid":"abe56ec4-248d-43b3-843e-35910f03d191","position":{"commit_sha":"6e4542f1e4f391a20b227676a488e83c51845b21","position":"1785772670464930001-abe56ec4-248d-43b3-843e-35910f03d191"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented + pushed as Gerrit change 1293 (commit 9d36af3d6b). All five prose blocks landed at their anchors: (18) 4a census self-contained; (19) test-design §6 config-effect contrast + synced copies; (20) 4b contention triggers routed by shape to two_clones/storm/reads-under-sync-contention by path; (21) 4g RED-test-first for behavioral gate findings; (22) Phase-5 residual-gap sweep + Reporting line. Sync gate 5/5 green. Dry-run: 9d7a caught by census dual-surface probe AND §6 contrast through the comment tool's real read path; ed2b matches trigger (iii) -> reads-under-sync-contention harness. Awaiting LLM-Review + Verified.","timestamp":1785772670464930001}],"created_at":1785640217627889001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"b2bd834b-520c-4e90-a53a-ebbf5f259fa2","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"c232-3a14-7bc9-4f68"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nFive approved prose upgrades to the implement-side skill and the shared test-design doc, targeting the largest escape classes: parity siblings at build time, config read-but-miswired, op-level contention semantics, gate findings fixed without oracle upgrades, and known gaps evaporating at close. (Bug-trend review changes 18-22; enforcement twins deliberately not proposed where FP modes dominate.)\n\n## Approach\nAll prose, no new gate machinery:\n(18) SKILL.md 4a surface-parity census, defined self-contained here (no equivalent exists yet in rebar-debug to inherit; sibling ticket 78f1 adds the debug-side analog independently): when the change touches one of several parallel surfaces, enumerate five slots — CLI / MCP-API / library-facade / automated-callers / dual-direction (reconcile read+write) — each slot dispositioned in-scope-and-proven-through-that-surface or out-of-scope-with-reason (feeds the Phase-5 sweep).\n(19) test-design.md §6 config-effect contrast: for each config key the change reads or should read, one test proving the key CHANGES BEHAVIOR through the real read path (default vs non-default contrast), not merely that a value is parsed — targets the read-but-miswired class (9d7a: honored by MCP server, ignored by comment tool).\n(20-prose) SKILL.md contention triggers, narrowed to op-level semantics (case c): if the change (i) composes >=2 locked operations or check-then-act across store reads/writes, (ii) adds its own retry/backoff/reclamation logic, or (iii) introduces a cache/snapshot over store state — add contention cases to the EXISTING shared suites by shape: composed/check-then-act writes -> tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py (two_clones fixture); write-storm/retry-reclamation -> tests/integration/test_store_concurrency.py (storm suite); read-integrity-under-contention (shape iii, the ed2b class) -> tests/interfaces/store/test_reads_under_sync_contention.py via the shared tests/interfaces/store/sync_contention_harness.py. 'Never a bespoke harness' means reuse these shared fixtures/harnesses — it does not claim no read-contention harness exists. Changes riding existing seams (single locked op) are exempt.\n(21) SKILL.md 4g gate-finding oracle upgrade: a behavioral gate finding gets a RED test FIRST in the same amended change, then the fix; non-behavioral (naming/docs/style) fixed directly — exemption stated to prevent change-detector tests.\n(22) Phase 5 + Reporting residual-gap disposition sweep over an enumerable source checklist (4a census out-of-scope slots, 4b exclusions, 4e-bis compromises, deferred 4g advisories): each item filed (ticket + discovered_from) / accepted-with-reason / fixed; 'none' legitimate.\n\n## Scope\n- examples/agent-skills/rebar-implement/SKILL.md (4a, contention trigger block, 4g, Phase 5, Reporting)\n- examples/agent-skills/shared/test-design.md §6 (+ sync of per-skill copies enforced by tests/unit/test_skill_shared_sync.py)\n\n## Testing\nProse-only: skill sync test must stay green (test_skill_shared_sync.py); dry-run read-through of the census + contention triggers against two historical bugs (9d7a config-miswire; ed2b pagination-under-writes).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] All five prose blocks landed at the named anchors; no new gate machinery introduced.\n- [ ] Contention trigger text scopes to the three case-c shapes and routes each shape to its existing shared suite by path (two_clones / storm / reads-under-sync-contention harness).\n- [ ] Shared test-design.md copies in sync (test green).\n- [ ] Census slots and disposition checklist use forced-artifact wording (in-scope-proven / out-of-scope-reason / filed / accepted / fixed).","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"examples/agent-skills/rebar-implement/SKILL.md","reason":"census/contention/oracle/disposition prose"},{"path":"examples/agent-skills/shared/test-design.md","reason":"config-effect contrast section"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","2f4c-7e5c-e782-4e97"],["relates_to","c232-3a14-7bc9-4f68"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2f4c-7e5c-e782-4e97","parent_status_uuid":"e897e6c0-85c2-4432-a5d0-3737739e6966","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["skills"],"ticket_id":"7359-5254-f634-48a3","ticket_type":"story","title":"rebar-implement skill + test-design: parity census, config contrast, contention triggers, oracle upgrades, residual-gap sweep","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["4357ec01-0a1d-4c4c-84f1-683fa7f04b95","ebb28ae6-11f1-4da9-a3ce-59e244f730d9","68ed0024-edc3-4b13-a792-074235e4b83e","4c8c18f1-0922-4f14-92e2-43a922f47895","e897e6c0-85c2-4432-a5d0-3737739e6966","2576303f-2238-4667-9215-17155e477a46","abe56ec4-248d-43b3-843e-35910f03d191","b2bd834b-520c-4e90-a53a-ebbf5f259fa2"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785773234263123525,"uuid":"80eff7f5-f107-41ee-ba32-7e90136af2da"}